"answer": "Project Zenith is a high-priority initiative aimed at driving innovation in data analytics and core operations, with a total approved budget of $2 million. The project kicked off on June 15th, led by Sarah Tan, with an initial phase one budget of $500,000. Key milestones include the completion of the design phase, the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, and the completion of the testing phase. The project is currently in Phase Two, where a breakthrough in predictive analytics has been achieved. Upcoming activities include a staff meeting on November 20th to share a detailed report, a call for feedback by the end of November, and a celebration of the testing milestone on October 10th. The project also involves potential partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology and focuses on leveraging AI for data visualization and UI enhancements."
